 height=3D"215"><br></div><div>The APB devices on this SoC are driven by th=
e PERIPH_CLK which can be derived from either the HCLK or the SYSCLK.</div>=
<div><br></div><div><img src=3D"cid:ii_l16t3sxv1" alt=3D"lpc32xx-clock.png"=
 width=3D"566" height=3D"364"><br></div><div>The default on reset is for PE=
RIPH_CLK to be derived from the SYSCLK but both U-Boot and Linux run in &qu=
ot;normal&quot; mode, which is to say that PERIPH_CLK, HCLK, ARM_CLK, and D=
DRAM_CLK are derived from the HCLK PLL.</div><div><br></div><div>There is n=
o separate SSP clock, the SSP is driven by one clock: the PERIPH_CLK (or &q=
uot;apb_pclk&quot;).</div></div></div>

